**Related human review quote** (from Tepaft7632.md - anomaly detection paper):
> "More comparison with the pretrained methods for TS anomaly detection should be discussed, such as TimesNet[1] and FPT[2]."

**Recommendation**: Include comparisons with additional parameter-efficient fine-tuning methods (prompt tuning, adapter layers, etc.) to better position CoRA in the broader adaptation landscape.

---

**Summary**: While CoRA presents a novel and promising framework for adapting time series foundation models to covariate-aware forecasting, the paper would benefit from: (1) stronger empirical validation of the Causality Embedding's alignment with Granger causality, (2) more comprehensive ablation studies, (3) statistical rigor in experimental reporting, (4) deeper analysis of when the method succeeds or fails, (5) computational cost analysis, and (6) broader baseline comparisons with other adaptation methods.
