**Applied to current paper:** While the paper states that "(i) conditioning on more properties improves performance, (ii) geometry-aware attention aids performance, and (iii) rollout resampling serves as effective regularization," these findings lack quantitative support in the main text. Detailed ablation tables showing performance with/without each component would clarify their individual contributions.
