## Weaknesses

1. **Limited comparison with stronger adaptive aggregation baselines**: While the paper compares against model averaging (Raza & Samothrakis 2019), Bayesian Model Averaging, and Super Learner, there is insufficient evaluation against more sophisticated ensemble methods that actively incorporate training information. As noted in similar work on reward model selection: *"The paper only compares LASeR with a simple offline RM Ensemble using averaged scores, despite the existence of more sophisticated ensemble methods"* (LASER review). The paper would benefit from comparisons with other theoretically-grounded aggregation schemes beyond simple averaging.

