<final_review>
## Weaknesses

1. **Limited Image Resolution and Benchmark Scope**: The paper evaluates on only AFHQv2 at 64×64 resolution, which is substantially lower than the capabilities of modern generative models. As noted in a related review: "FID may be unreliable here, as it relies on the Inception network... I recommend re-evaluating using DINO-FID to obtain a more accurate measure... The quantitative evaluations... are only conducted on 256×256 images, which is kind of low-resolution with respect to the capability of state-of-the-art diffusion models." Standard benchmarks such as CIFAR-10, ImageNet 256×256 or 512×512 are absent, limiting comparison with prior work.

   Quote inspiration: "The quantitative evaluations of REPA on DiT/SiT are only conducted on $256\times 256$ images, which is kind of low-resolution with respect to the capability of state-of-the-art diffusion models. I am wondering how REPA performs in higher-resolution cases, like $512\times 512$ which is also be supported by DiT/SiT. Is it still useful in training higher-resolution diffusion transformers?" — DJSZGGZYVi.md, Reviewer 3

2. **Insufficient Baseline Comparison on Standard Datasets**: The paper lacks solid comparison with prior methods on fundamental image generation tasks. One reviewer observed in a similar flow matching paper: "The proposed method achieved an FID of 8.45 on the CIFAR-10 dataset whereas the FM achieved a lower FID of 6.35... The authors should compare with FM on the CIFAR-10, ImageNet 32x32, the Oxford Flowers and the LSUN Church datasets." The current paper similarly omits comparisons on widely-established image benchmarks.

   Quote inspiration: "Although the tasks are diverse, the paper lacks a solid comparison with prior methods on some fundamental tasks. For instance, comparing LFM with Rectified Flow and OU diffusion on CIFAR-10 with the same amount of batches would offer a clearer understanding of LFM's training efficiency and distillation effects." — MM197t8WlM.md, Reviewer 2

3. **Limited Experimental Scope for Real-World Application**: The real-world evaluation is restricted to a single dataset (AFHQv2) at low resolution. As one review on a related generative model paper stated: "The experiments described in the paper are extremely limited. It is shown that 8 Gaussians can be generated using the proposed sampling method... For a publication to be recommended, the experiments should be expanded to include comparisons against relevant baselines." Similarly, the current paper's synthetic experiments on Gaussian mixtures and its single real-world dataset do not adequately demonstrate practical utility.

   Quote inspiration: "The experiments described in the paper are extremely limited. It is shown that 8 Gaussians can be generated using the proposed sampling method. Furthermore, in the paper, the sampling method was not compared to any other alternative method or ablated versions of the same method. For a publication to be recommended, the experiments should be expanded to include comparisons against relevant baselines." — WxLwXyBJLw.md, Reviewer 3
</final_review>
