4. **The claim that Social-R1-4B "surpasses LLaMA3-70B" is limited by the base model family.** The comparison is between Qwen3-4B (Social-R1) and LLaMA3-70B-Instruct (LLaMA3). A 4B model from the Qwen3 family cannot be directly compared to a 70B model from the LLaMA3 family without controlling for architecture, pretraining data, and instruction tuning differences. This makes the "18x fewer parameters" framing potentially misleading. Prior work has noted that "evaluation only on mathematical reasoning tasks" and experiments on "a single model family" limits the generalizability of claims (A6Y7AqlzLW review).
</final_review>
