5. **Cherry-picking evaluation metrics across datasets:** Similar to review (VB8xHF1Rdl.md) which states "cherry-picking the one task where it did work is not sound either. At the very least, some correction for multiple comparisons should have been made," the paper selectively highlights favorable results (e.g., highest Kendall-τ on RG-65, best ARI on clustering) without discussing where Omni-TM-AE underperforms or providing statistical significance testing across all datasets.
