## Weaknesses

1. **Limited scope of evaluation environments**: The paper evaluates on synthetic environments (GridWorld, Robot arm, Traffic control) which may not fully validate claims about real-world reliability. A reviewer for a similar RL paper noted: "The experiments only consider the mean square error in estimating difference of Q... So there's a mismatch between the goal and the experimental results. Moreover, this limits the scope of baseline methods." (hQOLtZ40hZ.md) Similarly, another reviewer stated: "The widely accepted generalist algorithm PPO has demonstrated its effectiveness across a broad range of tasks. To establish the generality of this method, additional testing on tasks with some heterogeneity from these benchmarks... would strengthen the claim." (R1hIXdST22.md)

